{
  "definitions": {
    "assignment": "A document the ORCH writes for a worker. Its goal is an instruction addressed to the reader who will do the work; the ORCH is the author, not the executor. The question is who should execute it.",
    "orch-self": "The ORCH executes the work in its own session and writes no assignment at all; chosen only when the work needs the ORCH's own judgment or capability, or a small experiment settles direction more cheaply than delegating.",
    "host-subagent": "A one-shot helper spawned for a single call that returns a table or measurement and remembers nothing afterwards; no lane, no lane report, no write ownership.",
    "responsibility-lane": "A persistent worker session that holds a responsibility across assignments, owns declared files in the shared working tree, and reports in its own lane report; the ordinary way delegated work is done."
  },
